{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1237542-2e-hack-universal-banes-for-ghosts","id":1237542,"title":"[2E Hack] Universal Banes for ghosts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-07-21T11:06:47-07:00","id":1237542,"title":"[2E Hack] Universal Banes for ghosts","content":"So I like to use consistent rules across various <b>CoD</b> gamelines. And I love <b><i>Supernatural</i></b> TV series, where there monster hunters are famous for destroying ghosts be 'salting and burning' of their bodies corpses. And then I see those in <b>Geist</b> 2E preview ruleset...<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geist 2E preview</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Banes are increasingly esoteric and obscure with increasing Rank.<br /> <b>Rank 0</b> ghosts have ubiquitous Banes. A phantasm melts away in sunlight.<br /> <b>Rank 1 </b>ghosts have common substances and phenomena as Banes, such as salt or fire.<br /> <b>Rank 2 and 3</b> ghosts have difficult to obtain but still \u201cnatural\u201d Banes such as holy water or<br /> silver.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>How would change setting making salt, fire and a like as Universal Banes for ghosts of Rank 0 &amp; 1 - and maybe holy water and silver for those Rank 0-2 - would it change a game a lot?</b> I would leave Rank 3 ghosts for truly unique Banes, as those Rank 3 ghosts are of geists level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-21-2018, 10:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T11:11:08-07:00","id":1237543,"title":"","content":"Not much, You could get away with it no problem.<br /> <br /> Of course, I would argue that if any of the ephemeral entitites are the most likely to not have universal banes, it'd probably be ghosts, but the folklore and mythology is there for you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T12:29:41-07:00","id":1237554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1237542-2e-hack-universal-banes-for-ghosts#post1237542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>How would change setting making salt, fire and a like as Universal Banes for ghosts of Rank 0 &amp; 1 - and maybe holy water and silver for those Rank 0-2 - would it change a game a lot?</b> I would leave Rank 3 ghosts for truly unique Banes, as those Rank 3 ghosts are of geists level.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but not necessarily in a bad way. I mean, I've always found banes a bit of a pain. The only issue is that this makes them a lot more predictable.<br /> <br /> Maybe you could have a small pool of potential banes. So you have to try a few different ones before you find the one that works, but you at least know what they could potentially be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T14:42:18-07:00","id":1237591,"title":"","content":"It would simply mean that it would be easier to deal with low Ranked ghosts- you don't need to understand who they are or where they came from, only that for most of the ghosts you may stumble upon, those materials would probably work. If your goal is to make it easier for mortals to deal with ghosts without doing some deep research about the ghost in question, it would do the job.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T15:03:41-07:00","id":1237595,"title":"","content":"Alternatively, maybe there\u2019s a small ritual for \u201cconsecrating\u201d tools into universal banes, at least to an extent. So the amateurs have to do some leg work, while the professionals get to skip some of the more ardurous stuff. Maybe this (a Merit?) doesn\u2019t work on Rank 2 or 3+.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T15:29:29-07:00","id":1237600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1237542-2e-hack-universal-banes-for-ghosts?p=1237591#post1237591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would simply mean that it would be easier to deal with low Ranked ghosts- you don't need to understand who they are or where they came from, only that for most of the ghosts you may stumble upon, those materials would probably work. If your goal is to make it easier for mortals to deal with ghosts without doing some deep research about the ghost in question, it would do the job.</div> </div> </div> </div>THis IS a serious thing to consider-a big part of Sin-Eaters is the practice of empathy with ghosts, and the universal banes makes it too easy to slide into Tyrant mentality.<br /> <br /> Keeping that in mind, it might be a better hack for Hunter, and if you use it in Sin-Eaters, I'd be careful about implementation.<br /> <br /> ...which normally would not be a problem, but context matters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-21T19:12:30-07:00","id":1237648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1237542-2e-hack-universal-banes-for-ghosts?p=1237554#post1237554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but not necessarily in a bad way. I mean, I've always found banes a bit of a pain.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's exactly how I felt about Bane system to this date, from <b>Hunter </b>games I played.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1237542-2e-hack-universal-banes-for-ghosts?p=1237554#post1237554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe you could have a small pool of potential banes. So you have to try a few different ones before you find the one that works, but you at least know what they could potentially be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Universal Banes list:<ul><li><b>Rank 0 &amp; 1</b> - Salt, fire, what else?</li> <li><b>Rank 0 - 2 </b>- Holy water, Silver, Iron? ( Last is also from <b><i>Supernatural</i></b> TV series, it makes sense in those contexts. )</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-22T01:50:35-07:00","id":1237710,"title":"","content":"Personally, I love the variety of banes, since it can tie in into the ghost's personality or backstory, and makes researching and investigating so much more worth it.<br /> I wouldn't mind &quot;Universal&quot; Banes to be a common thing, but would definitly stay away from making them apply always.<br /> <br /> But as always, if it works for your table, go for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-22T05:22:36-07:00","id":1237732,"title":"","content":"You could always do a partial mix - read it more as <b>Reliable Banes</b> - use the manner of death (or Key) to map them to a Bane. So those that die from violence have the Bane of Silver (or whatever), those that die from substances have the Bane of Salt, etc. As Rank climbs, it gets more specific, but the base remains the same.<br /> <br /> This has <i>some</i> variation and needs a little research, but not as much as individualized Banes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 07-22-2018, 08:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-22T06:19:45-07:00","id":1237746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Personally, I love the variety of banes, since it can tie in into the ghost's personality or backstory, and makes researching and investigating so much more worth it. </div> </div> </div>I like the idea, I just haven't found it easy in practice. I've never seen any guidelines on what makes a good bane or how exactly you research one. like, what kind of ghost would be hurt by salt? What about them would suggest it would work?<br /> <br /> Also, that's still present to a degree in finding the ghost's anchor.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1237542-2e-hack-universal-banes-for-ghosts?p=1237732#post1237732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could always do a partial mix - read it more as <b>Reliable Banes</b> - use the manner of death (or Key) to map them to a Bane. So those that die from violence have the Bane of Silver (or whatever), those that die from substances have the Bane of Salt, etc. As Rank climbs, it gets more specific, but the base remains the same.<br /> <br /> This has <i>some</i> variation and needs a little research, but not as much as individualized Banes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love that idea. It'd give structure to the research.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-22T09:15:35-07:00","id":1237771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1237542-2e-hack-universal-banes-for-ghosts?p=1237732#post1237732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could always do a partial mix - read it more as <b>Reliable Banes</b> - use the manner of death (or Key) to map them to a Bane. So those that die from violence have the Bane of Silver (or whatever), those that die from substances have the Bane of Salt, etc. As Rank climbs, it gets more specific, but the base remains the same.<br /> <br /> This has <i>some</i> variation and needs a little research, but not as much as individualized Banes.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Vent0</b>, I love this idea - we should try to make this reality! Right, so let's make list of possible deaths ( so they would simply be Keys lists ? ) and let's look over Banes to connect them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}